  "why_no_material_clear_new_design": "Existing design already transfers both terminal features from B to C and tests the local-versus-global crossing misconception. Changing the selected wire or subdividing those terminal edge groups repeats this hypothesis without new source information. The question has no independent input piece apart from the candidate wires, so an isolated single-wire color group would mainly create answer salience. A chord or second copy risks adding a puzzle wire or manufacturing a closure rather than styling the original. No simple materially different human-clear correspondence was found; no calls.",
